  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday) \nIssued at 1219 AM MDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nDaytime temperatures will continue well below average Fri/Sat\nbehind the strong backdoor cold front. A Freeze Watch may be\nrequired for Friday night for Union and Harding Counties. The\nretrograding upper low will pull up stationary offshore of the\nBaja Peninsula Saturday, steering moisture around it's broad\ncirculation into AZ and western NM where showers and a few storms\nare possible by Sunday. The upper low is modeled to fill an lift\nnortheast across the region as a shortwave trough Sunday night\ninto Monday, keeping chances for showers going. A more significant\nupper low will gather offshore of CA Tue/Wed and may bring a round\nof precipitation to NM Wed/Thu.",
